x_comment(x_argAndRestQuotedIsa,"A ternary #$ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.) used to place a specified quoted isa based argument-type constraint on a given #$VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number. (#$argAndRestQuotedIsa RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument to RELN must be a quoted instance of COL. Thus a closed formula (RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is a quoted instance of COL. See also argsQuotedIsa.") :- x_cid(a65b1270635ac6).
