x_comment(x_TextLearnerNCRuleEvaluationProcedure,"An instance of #$FullySpecifiedEvaluationProcedure and a sub-collection of #$Evaluating.  This collection represents a standardized procedure for evaluating instances of #$NounCompoundRule.  The evaluation works by sending several search strings to a search engine (typically,  the #$Google-SearchEngine) and recording the number of results.  More specifically, there are three related strings that are sent.  First, individual noun-compound phrases that are entailed by the rule are generated.  These phrases are individually tested and the number of hits for the phrases are recorded.  Secondly, the heads of the generated phrases are seperately queried and the number of their hits recorded.  Finally, the modifiers of the generated phrases are sent to the search engine and their individual hits are recorded.  The combined results of these can be stored in assertions using the predicate #$datedCandidateNCTestHasResults.") :- x_cid(a65b1270635ad5).
xc_microtheory(a65b1270635ad5,x_BookkeepingMt).
xc_source_file(a65b1270635ad5,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/fire/flat-files/nextkb/BookkeepingMt.krf').
xc_source_line(a65b1270635ad5,12080).
xc_kb_names(a65b1270635ad5,[]).
xc_mapping_rows(a65b1270635ad5,[]).
