x_comment(x_datedCandidateNCTestHasResults,"A sentence of the form (#$datedCandidateNCTestHasResults NC-RULE DATE RESULTS SEARCH-ENGINE) means that a group of candidate noun compounds were generated for NC-RULE on DATE and evaluated against the corpus covered by SEARCH-ENGINE with a result of RESULTS. In general,   RESULTS consist of list of lists where each element of the top-level list has the following form: (#$TheList  NC-STRING MOD-STRING HEAD-STRING MOD-TERM HEAD-TERM (#$TheList NC-HIT-COUNT MOD-HIT-COUNT HEAD-HIT-COUNT)). NC-STRING is a #$CharacterString that represents a particular noun compound that #$Cyc recognizes as satisfying the constraints of NC-RULE.  MOD-STRING and HEAD-STRING represent substings corresponding to the modifier and head of the compound (respectively).  MOD-TERM and HEAD-TERM are the denotations of MOD-STRING and HEAD-STRING wrt.which  NC-STRING is recognized as satisfying the constraints of NC-RULE.  NC-HIT-COUNT, MOD-HIT-COUNT, and HEAD-HIT-COUNT are the numbers of hits that were found by SEARCH-ENGINE for NC-STRING, MOD-STRING, and HEAD-STRING, respectively.") :- x_cid(a65b1270635adc).
xc_microtheory(a65b1270635adc,x_BookkeepingMt).
